  <running_head>Philosoph. Naturalis.</running_head>
  <bottom_margin>
    <catchword>DIS-</catchword>
    <signature>E 6</signature>
  </bottom_margin>
  <main_text>
    <l n="1">cedens patet, nam intensa vt octo di-</l>
    <l n="2">sponit vltimò materiam, &amp; præparat</l>
    <l n="3">ad formam; non sic intensa v. gr. vt</l>
    <l n="4">quatuor.</l>
    <l n="5" para="true">Respond. n. consequentiam, non</l>
    <l n="6">enim intensa qualitas habet gradus per-</l>
    <l n="7">fectiores, verùm plures; vndè perfe-</l>
    <l n="8">ctius agit, sicut validius operantur de-</l>
    <l n="9">cem homines, quàm octo, licèt singuli</l>
    <l n="10">sint æquales.</l>
    <l n="11" para="true">Obijcies 3. Si gradus intensionis om-</l>
    <l n="12">nino sunt similes, ergò qualitas auge-</l>
    <l n="13">ri poterit in infinitum, nam agens quo-</l>
    <l n="14">cumque gradu producto, valet producere</l>
    <l n="15">alium similem primo, non enim ad</l>
    <l n="16">hoc requiritur maior virtus.</l>
    <l n="17" para="true">Respond. n. antecedens. Ratio est,</l>
    <l n="18">nam etsi gradus parem habeant perfe-</l>
    <l n="19">ctionem, causa operans limitatur,</l>
    <l n="20">&amp; post multam actionem lassatur. Item</l>
    <l n="21">quia forma substantialis producenda</l>
    <l n="22">exigit certam, ac determinatam qua-</l>
    <l n="23">litatem. Tertio quia omne subiectum</l>
    <l n="24">est capax tot graduum qualitatis, non</l>
    <l n="25">plurium, &amp;c. Cum igitur causa ope-</l>
    <l n="26">rans limitatæ sit virtutis, atque se</l>
    <l n="27">accommodet exigentijs formæ,</l>
    <l n="28">subiectique, sistet aliquan-</l>
    <l n="29">do, nec vlterius pro-</l>
    <l n="30">cedet.</l>
    <l n="31" para="true">(*)</l>
  </main_text>
